# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Zola build output and search index
site/public/
site/static/processed_images/

# Custom
.DS_Store

# `just site-verify` generates one test per site code block and deletes the
# file again on success (scripts/site-verify.py).
tests/site_examples*.rs

# cargo-fuzz: build output, crash/timeout inputs, and generated corpus entries.
# Only the hand-named seeds under fuzz/corpus/<target>/ are committed; `just
# fuzz` writes new inputs to target/fuzz-corpus/ instead.
fuzz/target/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/

# The lock file the downstream-crate check (tests/macros.rs) resolves offline
tests/no_time_dep/Cargo.lock

# ── Internal notes and feature specifications ─────────────────────────────────

# Architecture notes (see concepts/README.md): the D/R-numbered decisions and
# risks, and ROADMAP.md, the spec of specs — every open item names its feature
# specification. Working documents, not claims this crate makes to its users:
# `site/` is the public narrative, `CHANGELOG.md` the history and the rustdoc
# the API contract. Nothing in the build reads them, and the `include`
# allowlist in Cargo.toml keeps them out of the package regardless.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that
# produces them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item (spec, plan, research,
# tasks), `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same
# rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published tree may not cite a path its
# reader does not have; `just concepts-check` fails on one that does. Matches
# billing, sepa, en16931 and agentplane.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
